<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sorrento</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Surrentum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sorrento is a town on the Sorrento Peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, overlooking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>. Known in antiquity as Surrentum, it was a self-governing duchy under Byzantine and Neapolitan influence in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> before falling to the Normans in the 12th century. It was the birthplace of the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torquato-tasso">Torquato Tasso</a> and is now a major tourist resort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sorrento.jpg" alt="Sorrento" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kim Traynor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Sorrento.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
